VISUAL QA
Viewed both attempts of each sheet, final contact, guides, upper strip and lower strip.
Correct two figures per sheet, true back, no handheld bow or loose arrow, neutral grey, no text/watermark. Skull uncovered, skeleton remains lean, ivory bones, olive-brown cloth, dark wood/leather quiver, rust nails and red accent retained. Broad form shading and dark folds retained, no glow, no added flesh or muscle, no microtexture or black cartoon outlines. Concept is also the applicable approved monster style reference.
Front/back retry substantially improves arm level and stance; numeric tolerances pass. There remains slight arm slope (2.1-2.5 degrees), and front feet turn outward slightly rather than perfectly parallel.
Side retry greatly improves foreshortening; hands overlap shoulders, far arms hidden, legs and feet overlap, no stride. Torso still reads mildly three-quarter rather than mathematically exact profile, with more chest visible than ideal. Side hand row approximately 20-21% versus front/back 19%, a small downward mismatch visible in guides.
Bone joints and skull remain stylized. Jaw has more separately indicated teeth than the canonical request for no detailed tooth rows. Visible nail-head count is about three per view; fourth/fifth required by canon is not clearly resolved. Band knot has a longer/two-point tie instead of the requested single short thick tie.

